-- Importer-view fixture — the backticked importer.
--
-- This sibling is read TEXTUALLY by the exporter's FIXTURE(d) scan when
-- interp-common.l4 is exported; it is what keeps `statute` alive there.
-- The backticked IMPORT spelling is the point of the fixture. (The IMPORT
-- sits before any § heading — after one, it stops resolving.)

IMPORT `interp-common`

GIVETH A NUMBER
use MEANS statute 5
